DatabaseGroups_Provision_MSSQL_AAG_DB_Ex.description:
Note: Order of backupNodeIds decides the priority of NDB backup preference

Provisioning into an existing Availability Group (AAG):
  - Set the 'dbserverLogicalClusterId' to the AAG's ID.
  - In the 'nodes' section, only include the 'dbserverId' for each node.
  - Rest of payload remains same.
  - `backupNodeIds` is required when dbgroup already has multiple AAGs or about to have multiple AAGs


Example:
```json
{
  // ... other fields
  "dbserverLogicalClusterId": "bd0e87af-56ca-4620-a9b8-23f8155e395a",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "dbserverId": "3c3717b7-3d11-4162-a3a0-824efa84b6c3"
    },
    {
      "dbserverId": "fdd3285f-505a-489d-a182-414b0638a6c9"
    }
  ]
}
